Date: Thu, 10 Sep 2026 16:45:36 +0800
Subject: [PATCH 093/250] feat(pypto-x): add qwen35 bf16 weighted execution
 driver and evidence audit

Driver (stages preflight/boundary-audit/s1/s2/s3/s4) binds the real
Qwen3.5-0.8B checkpoint through build_weight_mapping/build_weight_layout
(zero-copy mmap for the 284 conforming parameters, RNE materialization for
the 36 F32->BF16 regions), compiles the 6,710-plan model-profile T=5 graph
for AVX-512, and records per-operation timings, native/host_reference
boundaries, a real cgroup watchdog and an explicit --abort-op-mib guard.

S1 evidence: the pipeline compiles (lower 1.5 s, 6,710 plans) but the real
shape cannot execute -- op #4 (embedding) alone would materialize ~13.6 GiB
of Python lists because the AVX-512 host_reference path converts whole
tensors with _buffer_values/_buffer_from_values (avx2.py:366, avx512.py:265)
and launch keeps every SSA buffer alive (avx512.py:962). Retained-everything
peak is 7,660 MiB against the 8,192 MiB cgroup cap; the measured reference
throughput (6.58 MB/s, real AVX-512 artifact) projects 28.6 minutes for the
11.3 GB host_reference byte flow.

The evidence assembly script turns the raw step artifacts into
validation.json and copies the resource logs; no contract, Core IR or
artifact-version change is involved.
